            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "After buying the shirt, Ana retains $80\\%=\\frac45$ of the money remaining after buying the dress. This equals $\\frac23$ of her original money.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Fraction remaining after the dress}&=\\frac23\\div\\frac45\\\\\\text{Fraction remaining after the dress}&=\\frac56\\\\\\text{Fraction spent on the dress}&=1-\\frac56\\\\\\text{Fraction spent on the dress}&=\\frac16\\\\\\text{Original amount}&=\\$24\\times6\\\\\\text{Original amount}&=\\$144\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
